# tally 2.2.1 R20 (L §6.1 l.1802, OPERATIONS §2.1): a member's ask brings to the run's own level its refused scenario's
# line, its own when refused alone and its walk's warnings, never WARN-UNREAD, by the joint model's names, once per member;
# the lines under its result are the member's.
# 233.2: a member's ask refused alone prints its own line, the rest answers, exit 0. tally 2.2 refused the
# request REQ-ASK (T's held fixes/member-refused-alone).
=== options exit=0
=== jz.tally
model famz
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use c = "z/c.tally" sha256 "235dbf1f086762c2c3a59d08af4985e0421237bca1b3ce1f1d0ed7baf324d974"
=== z/c.tally
model cee
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "a card"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input pay: money PLN

input spare: num

def twice: money PLN = pay + pay at reader

ask q: twice law 2026-03-01





ask qw: twice with pay = 1 000.00 PLN law 2026-03-01

ask qk: twice law 2026-03-01 as known 2026-01-01



version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pay = 4 000.00 PLN "the card"

ask qnone: twice in zzz law 2026-03-01
=== expect c.qnone c.q
c.qnone: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO ask qnone names zzz, neither the model nor a loaded scenario (z/c.tally:35)
c.q: 8 000.00 PLN
  law date 2026-03-01, cut 2026-03-01
